Ten hexagons through every edge
===============================

The three-page manuscript proves the fixed source lower bound n(4,6,10)>=39.
Only order36 remains after the Moore exterior identity and hexagon divisibility.
The root traversal covers 18,351 deficit matrices, 310 matrix orbits and
3,565,944 normalized matching products. Each of 15,799 retained roots is
completed against each of the four possible three-edge exterior forests.
The complete boundary record has 63,196 calls and 182,532,443 nodes, with
no complete graph satisfying the root equations and girth restriction.

The new written argument proves the exterior reduction, exact normalization
under its forest automorphisms and joint choice of left/right attachments.
All right attachments remain unrestricted; ties between left masks imply no
additional right ordering. Every prune is a necessary condition. Acquired
root equations and the matching-forest theorem remain attributed and bound.

Replay with normal Python, clang++, 64-bit-word nauty, TeX and Ghostscript::

  python check.py --study STUDY --out FRESH_DIRECTORY --render

The default runs both complete target enumerations. The explicitly named
--reuse-recorded-targets mode instead verifies the exact successful input,
output and terminal-receipt closures, then repeats all bounded controls and
native builds. The initial separate-boundary timeout is preserved and gives
no exclusion. Three full control programs are also compiled with address
and undefined-behavior sanitizers; the full target uses the ordinary build.

The independent colour-orbit control covers all 236,196 assignments and
5,208 orbits; its suffix check covers 1,011,607 degree choices. The qualified
control field names distinguish nonisolated automorphisms and isolate
transposition generators from the full automorphism group order. The
original completed control and sole documentary rename remain preserved.

The known positive graph and 48 complete old/joint comparisons test literal
adjacency outputs. Four malformed inputs, two deadline checks and twelve
optimization guards reject invalid certificates. None substitutes for the
written completeness proof or the complete target calculation.

The sole native input of ten.tex is boundary_table.tex, supplied adjacent
and required by build_native.py. Source page18 is bound. The earlier author
wrapper omitted the graph argument to structural_control; its failed record
and exact earlier checker are development evidence, not a successful test.
The corrected wrapper has passed. Mathematical code and target bytes did
not change for that operational correction.

This recovers one already stated source lower-bound clause. It gives no
existence, uniqueness, new question, priority, whole-original, Lean or
compression-factor claim. Distinct review is required before acceptance.
